---
layout: layouts/admin.njk
pagination:
  data: consoleNav.areaTabs
  size: 1
  alias: tab
eleventyComputed:
  permalink: "{{ tab.url }}index.html"
  adminPage: "website"
  areaId: "{{ tab.area }}"
  areaTab: "{{ tab.tab }}"
  adminTitle: "{{ tab.label }}"
  areaLabel: "{{ tab.areaLabel }}"
  adminHeading: "{{ tab.heading | safe }}"
---
{#- AN AREA OF THE PUBLIC SITE'S WORK, ONE PAGE (Chase, 2026-09-27; split
   into four areas 2026-10-20, Website's own since 2026-10-21 —
   consoleNav.js `areas`): every tab of the area
   is here, and every tab's data loads when the page does — so moving between
   its tabs is instant, and an unsaved edit on one tab is still there after a
   look at another. Written at each tab's own address, opening on that tab,
   so a reload or a bookmark returns to where you were; admin-website.js
   moves between them without a reload and keeps the address in step.

   Each tab's markup is its own include (src/_includes/website/), and each
   tab's script finds its own elements, so the tabs do not know about one
   another — except for one thing, the site settings they share: see
   admin-website.js. -#}
{%- if tab.area == "creator" %}{% include "website/writing.njk" %}{% endif %}
{%- for t in consoleNav.areas[tab.area].tabs %}
<section class="web-panel" data-web-panel="{{ t.tab }}"{% if t.tab != tab.tab %} hidden{% endif %}>
  {% include "website/" + t.tab + ".njk" %}
</section>
{%- endfor %}

{%- if tab.area == "updates" %}
{#- PREVIEW ON A WEBSITE, as staff Updates has it (2026-10-27): the real
   widget beside the list (admin-library.js); Sharing has the code. -#}
<aside class="up-preview lib-preview" id="libPreview" hidden>
  <div class="emb-stagebar">
    <div class="emb-devices" role="tablist" aria-label="Width">
      <button type="button" class="emb-device is-on" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
              data-lib-width="wide" data-i18n="emb.desktop">Desktop</button>
      <button type="button" class="emb-device" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
              data-lib-width="narrow" data-i18n="emb.mobile">Mobile</button>
    </div>
    <span class="emb-scale-note" id="libScaleNote"></span>
    <span class="c-gap"></span>
    <select id="libLang" class="up-lang" aria-label="Language"></select>
  </div>
  <div class="emb-stage" id="libStage">
    <div class="emb-scale" id="libScale">
      <iframe id="libFrame" title="Preview" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>
    </div>
  </div>
  <a class="up-share-link" id="libShareLink" href="/admin/website/sharing/" data-i18n="up.shareLink">Share settings and code → Sharing</a>
</aside>
{%- endif %}
{%- if tab.area == "creator" %}
{#- Unsaved words and sections — on Pages, Navigation, Footer or Advanced:
   one bar for all of them, as the words are one set (admin-content.js).
   data-tabs says which tabs hold them, for the marks on the tabs
   (admin-website.js). -#}
<div class="ms-savebar" id="cSaveBar" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-tabs="pages" hidden>
  <span class="ms-dirty-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span id="cDirtyCount">0 unsaved changes</span>
  <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="cDiscard" data-i18n="ms.discard">Discard</button>
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="cSave" data-i18n="con.save">Save</button>
</div>
{%- endif %}

{#- The languages this build publishes, for Resources, Events and the contact
   form's reasons: the same list Eleventy paginated the public pages over, so
   the editor cannot offer a language the site does not render. -#}
{%- if tab.area == "updates" or tab.area == "sharing" %}
<script id="libLangs" type="application/json">{{ activeLangs | dump | safe }}</script>
{%- endif %}
